# Line endings, settled once for everybody.
#
# WHY THIS FILE EXISTS
#
# Every text file in this repository is stored with LF, because it was written
# on a Mac. Windows Git ships with `core.autocrlf=true` as its default, so a
# fresh clone on Windows gets CRLF in the working tree while the repository
# itself still holds LF. That is normally invisible — until something reads its
# own source.
#
# Several tests do exactly that. They lift a function out of public/app.js by
# finding the line containing only its closing brace, spelled as a newline, a
# brace and a newline. Under CRLF that never matches, and `npm test` stopped on
# "could not find the end of cropGeometry" before it had run a single check —
# on a checkout where nothing whatsoever was wrong with the code.
#
# Fixing it test by test would mean remembering to normalise in every future
# test that reads a source file, and the ones that forgot would fail only on
# Windows and only for whoever cloned rather than copied the folder. Settling it
# here fixes the class.
#
# WHAT ADDING THIS COST, ONCE
#
# Almost everything here was already LF, so almost nothing moved. Fourteen files
# were not: some SCSS, one built CSS bundle and a handful of SVGs under
# vesopa_web, all third-party assets that arrived with CRLF. Renormalising them
# is a diff of fifteen thousand lines that changes nothing —
# `git diff --ignore-cr-at-eol` over that commit is empty — and it is done once,
# here, rather than surprising whoever next edits one of them.

# Git decides what is text, and every text file is checked out with LF.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Windows-only files that genuinely want CRLF. A .bat or .ps1 read by an older
# tool can behave oddly without it, and neither is read by a test.
*.bat  text eol=crlf
*.cmd  text eol=crlf
*.ps1  text eol=crlf

# Left exactly as they are. `text=auto` detects most of these on its own, but
# being explicit costs nothing and a mis-detected certificate or font is a
# corrupted one.
*.png   binary
*.jpg   binary
*.jpeg  binary
*.gif   binary
*.webp  binary
*.ico   binary
*.pdf   binary
*.zip   binary
*.msix  binary
*.pkpass binary
*.p12   binary
*.cer   binary
*.crt   binary
*.ttf   binary
*.otf   binary
*.woff  binary
*.woff2 binary
*.mp4   binary
*.xlsx  binary
*.sqlite binary
*.db    binary
